{number: 57}
{title: We’ve a Story to Tell}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
We've a [C] story to tell to the [F] nations,
That shall [C] turn their hearts to the [G7] right,
A [C] story of truth and [F] mercy,
A [C] story of [G7] peace and [C] light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
For the [G7] darkness shall turn to [C] dawning,
And the [G7] dawning to noonday [C] bright,
And [C] Christ's great kingdom shall [F] come on earth,
The [C] kingdom of [G7] love and [C] light.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
We've a [C] song to be sung to the [F] nations,
That shall [C] lift their hearts to the [G7] Lord,
A [C] song that shall conquer [F] evil
And [C] shatter the [G7] spear and [C] sword.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
We've a [C] message to give to the [F] nations,
That the [C] Lord who reigneth a-[G7] bove
Hath [C] sent us His Son to [F] save us,
And [C] show us His [G7] heart of [C] love.
{end_of_verse}
